1
00:00:00,107 --> 00:00:04,987
When Persia became a serious threat,
Croesus turned to the gods for an answer.

2
00:00:05,412 --> 00:00:09,787
But first he decided to test the
famous oracles of the ancient world.

3
00:00:10,096 --> 00:00:12,787
He sent messengers to
several sacred sites and

4
00:00:12,787 --> 00:00:15,747
asked them what he was
doing on a particular day.

5
00:00:16,713 --> 00:00:19,327
At Delphi, the answer was astonishing.

6
00:00:20,019 --> 00:00:22,607
The priestess described
Croesus boiling a tortoise

7
00:00:22,607 --> 00:00:25,307
and a lamb together in a bronze cauldron.

8
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:28,227
That was exactly what he had been doing.

9
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:33,347
The test convinced Croesus that Delphi
truly possessed extraordinary knowledge.

10
00:00:34,012 --> 00:00:36,247
So he asked the question that mattered.

11
00:00:37,107 --> 00:00:38,647
Should he attack Persia?

12
00:00:39,398 --> 00:00:42,387
The oracle gave him an answer
that seemed almost perfect.

13
00:00:43,607 --> 00:00:47,827
If Croesus crossed the Halys River and
attacked, he would destroy a great empire.

14
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:50,707
Croesus assumed the great
empire meant Persia,

15
00:00:50,707 --> 00:00:53,127
and that assumption changed everything.
